    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e84734a4_3ab13607",
        "filename": "driver/mag_bmm150.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 82,
      "author": {
        "id": 1186109
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-29T02:52:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You said that drivers do not put sensor chips into FIFO mode, so for those boards that do not support a fifo in the EC (i.e. do not have CONFIG_ACCEL_FIFO defined), the FIFO size would effectively be 1 as there\u0027s no holding FIFO on the chip or in the EC, only what\u0027s read directly from the chip, thus the \"1\" setting since setup can only hold 1 sensor event.\n\nAt the board.c layer, when setting up motion_sensor_t structures, is where decision is made on a board-by-board basis as to whether to use this MAX_FIFO_EVENT_COUNT constant or, if CONFIG_ACCEL_FIFO is defined, to use CONFIG_ACCEL_FIFO.\n\nTo answer your question, this define will be used by all boards that do not support an EC FIFO (e.g. CONFIG_ACCEL_FIFO is not defined).",
      "parentUuid": "793588e0_5255124f",
      "revId": "3e9ab27f9181b05922320318e039f2df10ed897b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
